A||N||22||Quadfiero||Shocks/Struts opinions||||5||
Z||000000||Quadfiero||12-03-2000||10:41 PM||||I need to replace the shocks and struts on my daily driver '88GT. I would like something that will last and a good balance between ride and handling ( 60/40). I am looking at Konis. Any input would be appreciated.<BR>      Thanks,<BR>        Bob<BR>      '88 GT Quad 4 HO<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Black88GT||12-03-2000||10:48 PM||||I would say KONI's are way too pricey for just street driving.  I would go with KYB's, they are pretty cheap and provide what you are looking for.  However I have heard that they do not ride as well as the Monroe sensatracks, which are more expensive.<P>SO...<P>KONI's - handling<BR>KYBS'  - ride/handling<BR>Monroe - ride<P>IMHO<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-03-2000||11:31 PM||||I'm looking at the shocks and struts myself right now. the fronts are old but the rears are shot.<P>It also depends what monore product is involved. If some of their newer developments are available for Fiero then the handling advantage of KYB or even Koni in many applicaions may not be so great. <P>Monroe has recently moved some of their race technology to the street product. It gains considerable handling without the traditional ride loss.<P>Koni would still be there for full racing but for daily drivers the playing field is changing yet again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WisconsinGT||12-04-2000||02:16 AM||||I too have an 88GT for a daily driver. I put Monroe sensatracks on the car and have been very happy with the cars ride.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||12-04-2000||07:53 AM||||For daily driving, I have been happy with Gabriel.  They're probably softer than KYB, but half the price and available at Autozone.  However, they are gas-pressurized, so they raise the ride height slightly.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||12-04-2000||09:42 AM||||I've been very happy with KYB's on my 88 Coupe, and they don't feel much different after 50K miles than they did when they were new.||||reg||14
Z||000006||PearlBlueSoul||12-04-2000||03:06 PM||||Gotta say I like my KYBs.  nice n stiff w/o being too harsh.  After my spring job tho I don't think these struts can cut the butter.  I'm looking at Tokico blues or Illuminas (whichever I can afford first).  <P>I'd consider KYB or (if they make them) tokico blues.<P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff D.||12-04-2000||03:07 PM||||I vote -- KYB (affordable, driveable) sounds like what you need.||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||12-04-2000||05:14 PM||||I just put on Monroe sensatracks struts. Wow what a difference.  To top it off I only paid 88.56 for a pair with shipping & handling.  CarParts.com lists 56.85 each but with an online coupon I got 33% off.  You can't beat that for a great strut. I found the coupon at  <A HREF="http://www.coupons2001.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.coupons2001.com</A>  Try it, copy the code then go to carparts.com then to there coupon page and paste the code in and you get 33% of EVERYTHING except tires. Cool!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||webbee||12-04-2000||07:15 PM||||Haven't used the Monroe sensatracks. Have used the KYB and the Konis. For street I'd go KYB. For race Konis.||||reg||1
Z||000010||skitime||12-04-2000||07:21 PM||||I tried that carparts.com coupon number and it coming up expired.  It might be that I already used it and will not let me use it again.  Sorry, but you can try the other coupons.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||12-04-2000||09:36 PM||||Just do a search on <A HREF="http://www.dogpile.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dogpile.com</A>  for Carparts.com coupons.  You will find over 50 sites that offer them.<P>Also, they all say "first time customers only"  but I have ordered about 4 times from them with the same card/info., and I get the 33% off everytime.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||12-04-2000||11:28 PM||||I like the KYB's.  Haven't replaced the rear struts, but have them on the front and they seem great!  I am perfectly happy with the ride and they handle just fine for the local freeway ramps and such.||||reg||1
Z||000013||86_Fastback||12-05-2000||08:22 AM||||Go with KYB.  As everyone before has said, they are a good compromise between performance and ride.  I currently have KYBs and they were great with stock springs and pretty good with Eibach springs, but not good at all for a higher custom spring.  I t will be Koni for me in the near future.<P>-Gregg||||reg||1
Z||000014||bHooper||12-05-2000||09:44 AM||||MrPbody... how much do the gabrials affect ride height?  I am installing gabrials with eibachs on my GT.  Yeah, I know, shouldnt cut corners, but thought I would give them a shot.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">   <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||1
Z||000015||MrPBody||12-05-2000||08:50 PM||||bHooper --<P>Of course I didn't measure (that's way too professional), but I estimate 1/2".<P>-<P>On the original question --<P>According to AutoZone.com, Gabriels for an '88 are a bit more expensive than for '84-'87.  (That old '88 rarity problem.)  Maybe KYB's are the thing.  I would have bought KYB's for my car, except for price.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||bHooper||12-05-2000||09:49 PM||||well, obviously, you scared me enough about it.  if im going to pay the money to improve the apperance/ride height and handling... i don't want the struts jacking it back up!<P>thanks... only wish i new that 2 months ago when i started this whole project  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000017||MrPBody||12-06-2000||08:58 AM||||hoop --<P>Just to scare you further -- are KYB's also gas-pressurized?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||bHooper||12-06-2000||09:16 AM||||....?<P>yes, i guess they are.<P>oh well, i know i can live with this decision.<P>cause i ain't gonna spend no $150 per shock/strut for the koni's.<P>cant do it, just cant.....||||reg||1
Z||000019||Quadfiero||12-08-2000||02:19 PM||||Thanks for all the input guys! I think I am going to go KYB. Anyone know a good place to get them?<BR>     Thanks again,<BR>        Bob<BR>          '88 GT Quad 4 HO<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||bHooper||12-08-2000||03:40 PM||||i just ordered mine from Carparts.  See the following thread about my suspension rebuild.  It details all costs, sources and most coupons!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004682.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004682.html</A> <P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000021||Mark||12-08-2000||06:10 PM||||If you can't get a discount at Carparts.com, try tirerack.com.  If my memory is correct, their price on KYB's was much better than Carparts regular price, but a tad bit higher than the discount (33% off) price at Carparts.com.||||reg||1
Z||000022||JC Webb||12-09-2000||09:35 PM||||To those who have bought KYB struts, I pose this question:  Did the struts have holes or slots for the alignment bolts?  I am replacing my struts because my stock struts just have holes.  This does not allow me to adjust my rear camber.  I am tired of wearing out my Dunlop SP 8000's!<P>||||reg||1
